</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>How we marvel at this mercy</l><l>So far-reaching and so vast!</l><l>It has reached us, e’en the sinners,</l><l>And will ever hold us fast.</l><l>From this mercy, from this mercy,</l><l>What can cause us to be cast?</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>For Thy mercy we are grateful,</l><l>’Tis so rich, so plenteous!</l><l>Thru Thy mercy in redemption,</l><l>Thou hast richly favored us.</l><l>If without this, if without this,</l><l>How could we be favored thus?</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Oh, Thy mercy, so inspiring!</l><l>Gentle, tender, dear and sweet!</l><l>With Thy patience and Thy kindness,</l><l>Us in all our need it meets.</l><l>It we treasure, it we treasure,</l><l>Nothing can with it compete.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Father, we enjoy Thy mercy,</l><l>Ever fresh and ever new;</l><l>Every morning shed upon us,</l><l>It refreshes as the dew.</l><l>How we taste it! how we taste it!</l><l>Giving Thee the praises due.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>We can never cease to praise Thee,</l><l>As Thy mercy e’er endures;</l><l>All Thy grace and all Thy favor,</l><l>Ever for us it secures.</l><l>Trusting in it, trusting in it,</l><l>Thy sure mercy us assures.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
